ZVSE2
; WoG Debug - object visits: counts !?OB / !$OB triggers and remembers the last visit, so the command bridge can
; check them ("vars i wogdebug_visits wogdebug_postVisits wogdebug_type wogdebug_subtype wogdebug_x wogdebug_y
; wogdebug_hero"). Loaded only while WoG Debug is on. Every trigger is its own section, so each calls the function.

!?OB12;
!!FU(WogDebug_Visit):P;
!?OB53;
!!FU(WogDebug_Visit):P;
!?OB79;
!!FU(WogDebug_Visit):P;
!?OB101;
!!FU(WogDebug_Visit):P;

!$OB12;
!!VRi^wogdebug_postVisits^:+1;
!$OB53;
!!VRi^wogdebug_postVisits^:+1;
!$OB79;
!!VRi^wogdebug_postVisits^:+1;
!$OB101;
!!VRi^wogdebug_postVisits^:+1;

!?FU(WogDebug_Visit);
!!VRi^wogdebug_visits^:+1;
!!VRi^wogdebug_x^:Sv998;
!!VRi^wogdebug_y^:Sv999;
!!OB998:T?i^wogdebug_type^;
!!OB998:U?i^wogdebug_subtype^;
!!HE-1:N?i^wogdebug_hero^;
